The table structure information is (table names): 
['weekly_sales', 'shopping_cart_users', 'bitcoin_members', 'interest_metrics', 'customer_regions', 'customer_transactions', 'bitcoin_transactions', 'customer_nodes', 'cleaned_weekly_sales', 'veg_txn_df', 'shopping_cart_events', 'shopping_cart_page_hierarchy', 'bitcoin_prices', 'interest_map', 'veg_loss_rate_df', 'shopping_cart_campaign_identifier', 'veg_cat', 'veg_whsle_df', 'shopping_cart_event_identifier']
Begin Exploring Related Columns
Relevant tables / columns and how they will be used  

• shopping_cart_events.page_id : joins to shopping_cart_page_hierarchy so we know which product page the event belongs to; will also be filtered NOT IN (1,2,12,13).  
• shopping_cart_events.event_type : tells us whether the event was a Page View (=1), Add to Cart (=2) or Purchase (=3).  
• shopping_cart_events.cookie_id / visit_id : can be used if we later need to trace an individual journey.  
• shopping_cart_page_hierarchy.page_id : joins to shopping_cart_events.  
• shopping_cart_page_hierarchy.product_id : the “product” that we need to report on.  
• shopping_cart_page_hierarchy.product_category / page_name : optional descriptive columns for the final report.  
• shopping_cart_event_identifier.event_type / event_name : converts the numeric code (1‑3) into the textual label.  

Conditions that will be applied  

1. Exclude non‑product pages: WHERE sce.page_id NOT IN (1,2,12,13)  
2. Segment by event_type so we can count views, adds, purchases.  
3. “Left in cart” can be calculated as Adds – Purchases for every product_id.  

Below are 10 exploratory SQL statements (all limited to 20 rows) that move from simple inspection to the final aggregated result.  
Each query is preceded by a short description.

```sql
-- 1. List the distinct page_id values that appear in the raw events table
SELECT DISTINCT page_id
FROM shopping_cart_events
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. See how those page_id values map to products and categories
SELECT DISTINCT sch.page_id,
       sch.page_name,
       sch.product_category,
       sch.product_id
FROM shopping_cart_page_hierarchy AS sch
WHERE sch.page_id NOT IN (1,2,12,13)
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. Look at the three numeric event_type codes and their text names
SELECT DISTINCT sce.event_type,
       sei.event_name
FROM shopping_cart_events AS sce
JOIN shopping_cart_event_identifier AS sei
  ON sce.event_type = sei.event_type
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. Count “page views” (event_type = 1) per product_id
SELECT sch.product_id,
       COUNT(*) AS view_cnt
FROM   shopping_cart_events        AS sce
JOIN   shopping_cart_page_hierarchy AS sch
       ON sch.page_id = sce.page_id
WHERE  sce.event_type = 1
  AND  sce.page_id NOT IN (1,2,12,13)
GROUP  BY sch.product_id
ORDER  BY view_cnt DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5. Count “adds to cart” (event_type = 2) per product_id
SELECT sch.product_id,
       COUNT(*) AS add_cnt
FROM   shopping_cart_events        AS sce
JOIN   shopping_cart_page_hierarchy AS sch
       ON sch.page_id = sce.page_id
WHERE  sce.event_type = 2
  AND  sce.page_id NOT IN (1,2,12,13)
GROUP  BY sch.product_id
ORDER  BY add_cnt DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. Count “purchases” (event_type = 3) per product_id
SELECT sch.product_id,
       COUNT(*) AS purchase_cnt
FROM   shopping_cart_events        AS sce
JOIN   shopping_cart_page_hierarchy AS sch
       ON sch.page_id = sce.page_id
WHERE  sce.event_type = 3
  AND  sce.page_id NOT IN (1,2,12,13)
GROUP  BY sch.product_id
ORDER  BY purchase_cnt DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7. Aggregate all three counts together for each product_id
SELECT sch.product_id,
       SUM(CASE WHEN sce.event_type = 1 THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS view_cnt,
       SUM(CASE WHEN sce.event_type = 2 THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS add_cnt,
       SUM(CASE WHEN sce.event_type = 3 THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS purchase_cnt
FROM   shopping_cart_events        AS sce
JOIN   shopping_cart_page_hierarchy AS sch
       ON sch.page_id = sce.page_id
WHERE  sce.page_id NOT IN (1,2,12,13)
GROUP  BY sch.product_id
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8. Same as (7) but include the product name and category for readability
SELECT sch.product_id,
       sch.page_name,
       sch.product_category,
       SUM(CASE WHEN sce.event_type = 1 THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS view_cnt,
       SUM(CASE WHEN sce.event_type = 2 THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS add_cnt,
       SUM(CASE WHEN sce.event_type = 3 THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS purchase_cnt
FROM   shopping_cart_events        AS sce
JOIN   shopping_cart_page_hierarchy AS sch
       ON sch.page_id = sce.page_id
WHERE  sce.page_id NOT IN (1,2,12,13)
GROUP  BY sch.product_id, sch.page_name, sch.product_category
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9. Show events where products were added to cart but never purchased
SELECT sch.product_id,
       sch.page_name,
       COUNT(*) AS add_but_no_purchase
FROM   shopping_cart_events AS sce
JOIN   shopping_cart_page_hierarchy AS sch
       ON sch.page_id = sce.page_id
WHERE  sce.event_type = 2
  AND  sce.page_id NOT IN (1,2,12,13)
  AND  sch.product_id NOT IN (
        SELECT sch2.product_id
        FROM   shopping_cart_events AS sce2
        JOIN   shopping_cart_page_hierarchy AS sch2
          ON   sch2.page_id = sce2.page_id
        WHERE  sce2.event_type = 3
      )
GROUP  BY sch.product_id, sch.page_name
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10. Final consolidated report: views, adds, purchases, left‑in‑cart
SELECT sch.product_id,
       sch.page_name,
       sch.product_category,
       SUM(CASE WHEN sce.event_type = 1 THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS view_cnt,
       SUM(CASE WHEN sce.event_type = 2 THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS add_cnt,
       SUM(CASE WHEN sce.event_type = 3 THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS purchase_cnt,
       SUM(CASE WHEN sce.event_type = 2 THEN 1 ELSE 0 END)
       - SUM(CASE WHEN sce.event_type = 3 THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS left_in_cart_cnt
FROM   shopping_cart_events        AS sce
JOIN   shopping_cart_page_hierarchy AS sch
       ON sch.page_id = sce.page_id
WHERE  sce.page_id NOT IN (1,2,12,13)
GROUP  BY sch.product_id, sch.page_name, sch.product_category
ORDER  BY view_cnt DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

